<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Felix and Regula</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 300</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Saints Felix and Regula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Felix and Regula are the patron saints of Zürich, a brother and sister said by legend to have been soldiers of the Theban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> who fled to Zürich and were beheaded there for their Christian faith around 300. Their cult developed in the Carolingian period around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grossmunster">Grossmünster</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fraumunster">Fraumünster</a>, and they appear on the seal and arms of the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/felix-and-regula.jpg" alt="Felix and Regula" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zürcher Veilchenmeister · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Altartafel_Kapelle_Spannweid_Z%C3%BCrich_Stadtheilige.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
